{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.UnitModulusEigenvalue","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.UnitModulusEigenvalue","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Int.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Units.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.GroupWithZero.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.borromean_eigenvalue_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.borromean_eigenvalue_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/UnitModulusEigenvalue.lean#L92-L115","doc":"**Borromean eigenvalue is `−1`.** If `λ` is an eigenvalue of\n`ρ_{(2,1)}(β_Bor)` — a root of the `2×2` characteristic polynomial\n`λ² − tr·λ + det` with the Borromean data `tr = −2`, `det = 1` —\nthen `λ = −1` (the degenerate fixed point).\n\nThe characteristic polynomial is `(λ + 1)²`, so the only structure the\nargument uses is the absence of zero divisors:\n`(λ + 1)² = 0 ⇒ λ + 1 = 0 ⇒ λ = −1`.  §7c: stated over\n`[CommRing R] [NoZeroDivisors R]` rather than `[Field R]` — the weakest\nclass that admits it.  `NoZeroDivisors` is not removable: over\n`ZMod 4`, `λ = 1` satisfies `λ² + 2λ + 1 = 0` but `λ ≠ −1`.\nThe data `tr = −2` is the Hoefsmit / Markov-trace input (carried as\na hypothesis, not asserted here); `det = 1` is `even_braid_det_one`\nfor the 6-generator word. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:unit-modulus-eigenvalue","label":"prop:unit-modulus-eigenvalue","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unit-modulus-eigenvalue.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.even_braid_det_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.even_braid_det_one","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/UnitModulusEigenvalue.lean#L82-L88","doc":"A product of an even number `2k` of Hecke generators on `V_{(2,1)}`\nhas determinant `(−1)^{2k} = 1` (each generator contributes `−1`).\nTogether with `|tr| ≤ 2` this is the unit-circle condition\n`λ₁λ₂ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.hecke_generator_det_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.hecke_generator_det_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/UnitModulusEigenvalue.lean#L66-L78","doc":"The Hecke relation `σ² = h·σ + 1` forces `det(σ) = −1` on every\n2-dimensional Wedderburn block: the eigenvalues of `σ` are `q` and\n`−q⁻¹` (roots of `x² − h·x − 1`), with product `q·(−q⁻¹) = −1`.\n\n§7c: a **units** identity over a plain `CommRing` — the second\neigenvalue is only defined when `q` is invertible, so `q` is carried as\n`q : Rˣ` and the inverse is `Units.inv`. Over a field this is exactly\nthe old `q ≠ 0`; unlike the field version it also applies over\n`ℤ[q, q⁻¹]`, where `q` is a unit but no division is available. ","signatureChunk":0}]}